# inbox's routes (core/modules/inbox/README.md "API"): a member's session, inbox.read to read the
# threads and a thread, inbox.label to label a reply of a thread of your own with one of the 7 labels
# (gamma-p4-055; more cases in gamma-p4-055-confirm-label.http). Only the conversations the platform
# started are there, and no route here sends: a reply from a thread is
# gamma-p4-060-reply-from-inbox.http.
# The label's PUT sets a state, so it takes no Idempotency-Key; it sends the cookie, so it sends
# Origin: {{appOrigin}} too. `threadId` is a thread of yours, on the LinkedIn account you connected,
# and `messageId` a reply in it: put them in http-client.private.env.json with your workspaceId.
# Every answer is the caller's own (gamma-p6-060): the list holds the threads of your own accounts
# only, whatever your role, and another member's thread or message answers 404, as another
# workspace's does.

### GET /v1/workspaces/{workspaceId}/inbox/threads: your own threads, newest first, 50 a page at most, each with its lead, the time of the last message, who wrote last and the replies to label; nextCursor for the next page
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/workspaces/{{workspaceId}}/inbox/threads?limit=20
Accept: application/json
Cookie: {{sessionCookie}}

### GET /v1/workspaces/{workspaceId}/inbox/threads/{id}: the thread, its lead and its messages oldest first, each reply with its label or null, each reply from the inbox with its send's status and code; whether you reply on it; 404 thread_not_found (another member's too)
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/workspaces/{{workspaceId}}/inbox/threads/{{threadId}}
Accept: application/json
Cookie: {{sessionCookie}}

### PUT /v1/workspaces/{workspaceId}/inbox/messages/{id}/label: labels a reply of your own thread with one of the 7 labels, or changes its label, and runs the label's action on the person's newest reply; 200 with the label, its class and beta's word; 409 message_not_inbound for a message the account sent, 404 inbox_message_not_found (another member's too)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/v1/workspaces/{{workspaceId}}/inbox/messages/{{messageId}}/label
Accept: application/json
Content-Type: application/json
Cookie: {{sessionCookie}}
Origin: {{appOrigin}}

{ "label": "interested" }
